    == PHASE 6 — Pre-merge handoff (Phase 7.2) + absorb (Phase 4) + terminal ack
                (Phase 7.1) ==

    This is the big one — exercises three Phase 7 features in sequence.

      6a. PRE-MERGE HANDOFF (7.2):
          sme-auth-1 (mutation POC) MUST raise a clarification to sme-auth-2
          BEFORE absorb_agent:
            create_clarification(asker=sme-auth-1, responder=sme-auth-2,
              question_message="Pre-merge handoff: I'm about to absorb you. Brief me
              on configs / runtime nuances / monitoring quirks NOT in your
              component_doc_md / source_slice / attributions / edges / flows.
              Respond with QC.")
          sme-auth-2 responds with QC and a one-paragraph brief mentioning at least
          one nuance (e.g., "deploy needs special env var AUTH_SECRET_KEY; on-call
          rotation in pagerduty schedule SCHED-123").
          sme-auth-1 reads the response and updates its own component_doc_md via
          upsert_component to capture the brief.

          REPORT [DEMO7-OK] if handoff happened in this order; [DEMO7-FAIL] if
          sme-auth-1 absorbed without the clarification.

      6b. ABSORB (4.1 cascade):
          sme-auth-1 calls absorb_agent(consolidation_id, target=sme-auth-2,
                                        deactivation_reason='merged',
                                        deactivation_notes='auth-svc-v2 folded in')
          with default cascade flags.

          Verify:
            - sme-auth-2.status = 'decommissioned'
            - sme-auth-2.merged_into_agent_id = sme-auth-1
            - sme-auth-2's attributions transferred to sme-auth-1's component
            - sme-auth-2's component status = 'decommissioned'

      6c. EXECUTE + COMPLETE (Phase 4):
          sme-auth-1 calls execute_mutation → status M → MD.
          Resolver calls complete_consolidation → status MD → D.

      6d. TERMINAL ACK (7.1) — the new behaviour:
          After complete_consolidation, the consolidation status is D. Both
          sme-auth-1 (still active) AND resolver should now have this consolidation
          in their `terminal_pending_ack` bucket. Verify by:
            - sme-auth-1 calls get_action_items_summary → terminal_pending_ack > 0
            - resolver calls get_action_items_summary → terminal_pending_ack > 0
            - Each calls ack_terminal('consolidation', consolidation_id).
            - Re-call get_action_items_summary → terminal_pending_ack drops to 0.

          Verify decommissioned sme-auth-2 was AUTO-ACKED via absorb_agent (i.e.,
          a row exists in terminal_acks for sme-auth-2 even though it never
          explicitly acked).

          REPORT [DEMO7-OK] for each verification step.

